 @drakuldxd  Fake Framerate is the definition of what it's doing. It is creating fake frames in-between the actual frames to fill in the gaps using AI. They are not "actual" frames. Think of them more so as a "filler" to help improve image quality with the cost of increasing latency, whereas, adding additional frames where none exist means the time between what's actually happening and what's displaying on your screen is increased. It is not actually increasing performance or giving higher quality. So, at the end of the day, based on the graphs shown in the video when you purchase this card. You are essentially getting a worse 3060 that uses AI to add in "Fake Frames" when you use DLSS3. Which, again, is barely supported as only a few handfuls actually have Official DLSS3 Support.

In short, if you turn DLSS3 off, those are the actual frames you are getting and the true performance of the card. Which, will be the performance you get with ANY game that does not support DLSS3. 

Small Edit: I currently use 2 different machines. My Main rig which has 13900KS + RTX 4090 and my work rig which runs a 12700K and RTX4080 16G. So this is coming from a user of the Generation. And I will be the first one of us to fully admit, this generation is a rip off. Instead of actually increasing performance, they are saving a quick buck by using AI to cheat extra frames in, which as stated are not always perfect and then charging a premium exalting the DLSS3 feature that only exists on a very short list of titles.

